// Park
// Source: /Docs/API-endpoints/13-social-endpoints.md §5-7
//
// A temporary shared space. Somebody opens one, other people's creatures walk
// into it, and when the last person leaves it stops existing.
//
// Why a table at all, for something temporary
// -------------------------------------------
// Three of a park's facts have to be answered by something other than a live
// socket, and each one is a security decision rather than a convenience:
//
//   capacity      enforced by a row lock on THIS row inside the joining
//                 transaction, which is what makes "the last free slot" safe
//                 when two people race for it (see parks.service.ts)
//   the passcode  a private park's credential is a scrypt hash, and a hash held
//                 only in a process's memory is a hash that a restart turns
//                 into "anyone may enter"
//   discovery     a list of parks has to survive the moment between one client
//                 creating one and another client asking what is open
//
// What is NOT here is presence: where a creature is standing, what it is doing
// and which way it is facing are per-frame facts. They live in the gateway's
// memory and are never written down (10-realtime-events.md §1).
//
// Lifecycle: `ParksService.sweep()` deletes parks nobody is in, on an interval
// and on boot. Nothing here is expected to outlive the people in it — see the
// note on `ParkParticipant.lastSeenAt`.

model Park {
  id     String @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  hostId String @db.Uuid

  /// What it is called in the list. 1-40 chars.
  name String

  /// How many creatures may be in it at once, including the host's.
  capacity Int @default(6)

  /// `public` | `private`.
  ///
  /// A public park is listed and joinable by anyone signed in. A private one is
  /// listed by name only — never with its credential — and needs the passcode.
  visibility String @default("public")

  /// scrypt hash of the passcode, or null for a public park.
  ///
  /// Never leaves the backend. No route, view or socket payload includes this
  /// column, and `toParkView` is built field by field rather than by spreading
  /// the row, so a column added later cannot leak by being forgotten about.
  passcodeHash String?

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())

  host         User              @relation(fields: [hostId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  participants ParkParticipant[]
  messages     ParkMessage[]

  /// The list query: open parks, newest first.
  @@index([visibility, createdAt])
  @@index([hostId])
}
